"run_roman_self_healing_concrete_1793161347": [
"Modern concrete",
"structures can begin",
"to crumble just",
"a few decades",
"after construction,",
"yet Rome’s Pantheon,",
"dedicated in AD 128,",
"still stands intact",
"with the world's",
"largest unreinforced",
"concrete dome.",
"Ancient Roman",
"aqueducts continue",
"to deliver water",
"to Rome",
"today, enduring",
"some two millennia",
"through volcanic",
"pozzolans.",
"Chemical analysis",
"of materials",
"from Pompeii",
"demonstrated builders",
"used a hot-mixing",
"process with quicklime",
"to produce self-healing",
"properties, overturning",
"longstanding assumptions",
"based on ancient",
"texts of Vitruvius.",
"Today, petrographic",
"analysis of ancient",
"concrete provides",
"critical evidence",
"for developing",
"modern sustainable",
"building materials.",
"Ancient Roman",
"structures endure",
"while modern",
"engineering crumbles",
"in decades."
],
