"run_singing_colossi_of_memnon_1792952878": [
"In 27 BC,",
"a major earthquake",
"shattered the northern",
"colossus, collapsing",
"the statue",
"from the waist",
"up and cracking",
"its lower half.",
"Following",
"the earthquake damage,",
"the northern",
"monument became",
"famous throughout",
"the ancient world",
"for emitting a reported",
"cry at dawn.",
"Reaching a total",
"height of 60 feet",
"including their 13-foot",
"pedestals, each",
"colossus weighs",
"an estimated 720 tons.",
"The last reliable",
"historical record",
"of the statue",
"vocalizing dates",
"to the year",
"196 AD.",
"Local tradition dates",
"the reconstruction",
"of the statue's",
"upper tiers",
"to around 199 AD.",
"Still, the colossi",
"have stood",
"since 1350 BC,",
"originally carved",
"to guard the memorial",
"temple where Amenhotep",
"the Third",
"was worshipped."
],
"run_trepanation_miracle_1792995462": [
"Trepanation is the oldest",
"documented surgical",
"procedure in human",
"history, dating back",
"between 7,000 and",
"10,000 years ago.",
"Ancient Peruvian",
"surgeons demonstrated",
"advanced technique",
"by avoiding the midline",
"of the skull,",
"which prevented lethal",
"damage to the cerebral",
"sagittal sinus.",
"Physical evidence",
"suggests prehistoric",
"trepanation served",
"as emergency surgery",
"following trauma",
"to extract shattered",
"bone fragments",
"and clean out",
"pooling blood.",
"Ancient societies also",
"operated for spiritual",
"motives such",
"as releasing evil",
"spirits, or treating",
"mental disorders",
"and epilepsy.",
"By one",
"estimate, advancements",
"in Peruvian surgical",
"technique contributed",
"to cranial surgery",
"survival rates",
"climbing over time",
"to 80 percent.",
"Signs of the bone",
"healing process confirm",
"that patients survived."
],
"run_tunguska_event_1908_1792930600": [
"On the morning",
"of 30 June 1908",
"at around 7:14",
"local time,",
"near the",
"Podkamennaya Tunguska",
"River in Central Siberia,",
"a cataclysm struck",
"By one estimate,",
"the blast devastated",
"more than 830 square",
"miles of taiga forest,",
"flattening trees",
"in a distinctive",
"radial pattern.",
"Scientists calculate",
"the airburst released",
"between 10 and 15",
"megatons of TNT.",
"Atmospheric pressure",
"waves generated",
"by the explosion",
"rippled across the globe",
"and were detected",
"by barographs",
"worldwide.",
"Scientific consensus",
"attributes the event",
"to an atmospheric",
"meteor air burst,",
"though no celestial",
"fragment has ever",
"been formally identified",
"from that sudden",
"Siberian morning."
],
"run_unfinished_obelisk_aswan_1792985912": [
"Deep in Egypt’s Aswan",
"quarries lies a granite",
"monolith that would",
"have been nearly",
"one-third larger",
"than any obelisk",
"ever erected.",
"Ancient workers",
"burned and wedged",
"away upper rock,",
"carving directly",
"into bedrock",
"where tool marks",
"and ochre lines",
"still mark the trench.",
"Surveys place",
"the completed",
"monument's",
"length between",
"roughly 41.75 metres",
"and 42 metres,",
"while calculations",
"of the finished",
"obelisk's weight range",
"from nearly 1,090",
"tonnes to 1,168 tonnes.",
"Modern engineering",
"studies cannot establish",
"whether moving",
"the monolith",
"was within structural",
"limits of granite",
"before multiple",
"fissures cracked",
"the stone.",
"Attached to the bedrock,",
"this unfinished giant",
"preserves ancient",
"Egypt's grandest quarry."
],
"run_unfinished_obelisk_aswan_1792993374": [
"Deep inside an ancient",
"Aswan granite quarry,",
"Egyptian builders",
"carved a colossal",
"monolith directly out",
"of solid bedrock",
"that remains trapped",
"in the earth today.",
"Quarry workers",
"burned and wedged",
"away upper rock",
"layers, flattening",
"the stone",
"while leaving red",
"ochre cut lines",
"along the deep trenches.",
"Surveys place",
"the completed",
"monument's length",
"between roughly 137",
"and 138 feet,",
"with finished weight",
"calculations ranging",
"from nearly 1,090 to 1,168",
"tonnes.",
"When structural",
"cracks appeared,",
"the project",
"was abandoned.",
"Modern engineering",
"studies still have",
"not established",
"which extraction",
"method was intended,",
"leaving this unfinished",
"giant locked forever",
"in the bedrock."
],
"run_unfinished_obelisk_aswan_1793056896": [
"Deep inside an ancient",
"quarry in Aswan,",
"the largest obelisk",
"ever attempted",
"remains trapped",
"in solid bedrock.",
"Workers burned",
"and wedged away",
"upper rock,",
"carving trenches",
"where visible tool",
"marks and ochre",
"lines still mark",
"their cuts.",
"Surveys place",
"its length between",
"roughly 137 feet",
"and 138 feet,",
"with weight",
"calculations ranging",
"from nearly 1,090",
"tonnes to 1,168 tonnes.",
"Work was abandoned",
"after structural",
"cracks and multiple",
"fissures appeared.",
"Modern engineering",
"studies cannot confirm",
"which extraction",
"method was intended,",
"or whether moving",
"the monolith",
"was within granite's",
"structural limits.",
"These deep fissures",
"left Egypt's greatest",
"monument forever",
"anchored in the stone."
],
"run_voynich_manuscript_1792965308": [
"An unread medieval",
"book displays",
"linguistic precision",
"that defeats",
"modern cryptanalysis.",
"Radiocarbon dating",
"established",
"that the manuscript's",
"parchment dates",
"between 1404 and 1438.",
"By one estimate,",
"the text is written",
"from left to right",
"in an unidentified",
"script where an alphabet",
"of 20 to 25",
"characters accounts",
"for virtually",
"the entire work.",
"Beside botanical",
"diagrams of unidentified",
"plants, the text",
"conforms to Zipf's law",
"where the most",
"common word appears",
"roughly twice as often",
"as the second",
"most common.",
"The manuscript",
"is named after Polish",
"book dealer",
"Wilfrid Voynich,",
"who acquired it",
"in 1912.",
"American and British",
"military cryptographers",
"from both World War",
"One and World War",
"Two attempted",
"to decipher the codex",
"without success."
],
"run_wieliczka_salt_mine_1792974672": [
"Near Kraków",
"in southern Poland,",
"the mine's rock",
"salt naturally",
"displays various",
"shades of grey,",
"resembling unpolished",
"granite rather",
"than white",
"crystalline salt.",
"Engineering surveys",
"and heritage records",
"place the total extent",
"of underground galleries",
"between 287 and 300",
"kilometers.",
"By one estimate,",
"underground miners",
"carved four chapels",
"and dozens of statues",
"directly out",
"of the native",
"rock salt.",
"Wieliczka was",
"designated as one",
"of the original",
"UNESCO World Heritage",
"Sites in 1978.",
"Artificial ventilation",
"introduced in the late",
"nineteenth century",
"brought humidity",
"into the mine,",
"threatening severe",
"damage to the carved",
"salt sculptures.",
"Today, the subterranean",
"chapels feature",
"chandeliers carved out",
"of natural rock salt."
]
